<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply rises in October.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply rises in October.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply rose by C$1.39 billion to C$65.62 billion in October from C$64.23 billion in September and compared with C$59.07 billion in October 1995, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					   Oct 96    Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p>M1					 65.62	64.23	59.07</p>
<p>M2					393.28     390.76     384.00</p>
<p>M3					492.34     485.18     466.54</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Chartered bank assets			    Oct	  Sept</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-12.92	-12.67</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     657.76	653.27</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    104.65	102.90</p>
<p>				    Wk to Nov 20  Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.935  -0.461     +0.519</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     7.930  -0.842     -3.810</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	465.745  +0.097     +6.436</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 144.100  -2.700    -21.300</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.919  +0.397     +2.213</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745</p>
</text>
